      <h2 id="cutoffs" class="text-3xl font-bold mt-12 mb-6">Manitoba PNP Score Cutoffs by Selection</h2>

      <p>
        A single "Manitoba PNP cutoff" doesn't exist. Each selection draws from a different slice of the pool, so the minimum score only means something next to the group it applies to. Here are the score-based selections from the table above:
      </p>

      <div class="overflow-x-auto my-8">
        <table class="w-full text-sm border border-slate-200 rounded-xl">
          <thead class="bg-amber-50">
            <tr>
              <th class="p-3 text-left">Date</th>
              <th class="p-3 text-left">Selection (Skilled Worker in Manitoba)</th>
              <th class="p-3 text-left">LAAs</th>
              <th class="p-3 text-left">Lowest score invited</th>
            </tr>
